{"ref": "Makkot 5a:8", "heRef": "מכות ה׳ א:ח׳", "sectionRef": "Makkot 5a", "indexTitle": "Makkot", "heIndexTitle": "מכות", "categories": ["Talmud", "Bavli", "Seder Nezikin"], "next": "Makkot 5b", "sectionNames": ["Daf", "Line"], "versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Wikisource Talmud Bavli", "license": "CC-BY-SA", "versionSource": "http://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%AA%D7%9C%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%93_%D7%91%D7%91%D7%9C%D7%99", "text": "<big><strong>גמ׳</strong></big> מנא הני מילי אמר רב אדא דאמר קרא (דברים יט, יח) והנה עד שקר העד שקר ענה עד שתשקר גופה של עדות"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "Sefaria Community Translation", "license": "CC0", "versionSource": "https://www.sefaria.org", "text": "GEMARA: From ever do we know these words [that witnesses need to be personally disqualified to become zomemim]?  Rav Ada says, The Torah says, (Deuteronomy 19: 18) \"And behold, a false witness, he has testified falsely\", [we derive that they doesn't become zomemim] until the body of the testimony [the witnesses themselves] get contradicted."}], "available_versions": [{"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "license": "CC-BY-NC", "versionSource": "https://korenpub.co.il/collections/the-noe-edition-koren-talmud-bavli-1"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actualLanguage": "en", "versionTitle": "William Davidson Edition - English", "license": "CC-BY-NC", "versionSource": "https://korenpub.com/collections/the-noe-edition-koren-talmud-bavli-1"}, {"language": "he", "languageFamilyName": "hebrew", "actualLanguage": "he", "versionTitle": "Wikisource Talmud Bavli", "license": "CC-BY-SA", "versionSource": "http://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%AA%D7%9C%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%93_%D7%91%D7%91%D7%9C%D7%99"}, {"language": "en", "languageFamilyName": "english", "actua